      "side": 1,
      "message": "I believe it is a further discussion from [here](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/45931#discussion_r880374185). Regarding putting a `GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH` flag, it might be more confusing. I have a [discussion](https://github.com/zephyrproject-rtos/zephyr/pull/45931#discussion_r888459429) with Keith during code review. In npcx datasheet section 4.8.1., it describes \u0027A transition from 0 to 1 of GPIO85 data-out bit 5 in P8DOUT register indicates a firmware request to dessert PSL_OUT. (I have added a comment in cros_system_npcx.c) Actually, PSL_OUT is low in inactive mode and is the opposite of `GPIO_ACTIVE_HIGH`\n\nRegarding fixed \u0027enable-gpios\u0027 node, I have moved it to \u0027zephyr/boards/arm/npcx9/npcx9.dts\u0027, \u0027zephyr/boards/arm/npcx7/npcx7.dts\u0027, `zephyr/boards/arm/npcx_evb/npcx7_evb`, and `zephyr/boards/arm/npcx_evb/npcx9_evb` in its parent CL.\n\nRegarding `pinctrl-names` DT node, usually, `pinctrl-names` and `pinctrl-x` are pairs for pinctrl mechanism. Putting it and pinctrl-0 property together has a better understanding.",
